89412.163622   ALWAYS ASKS YOU FIRST
89412.163624     bash     Run one command line through bash — really bash, including on Windows, where it is Git Bash.
89412.163626     (and any network request, per host, every time)
89412.163627 
89412.163628   MAY ACT WITHOUT ASKING
89412.163629     ask      Put a question to the user and wait.
89412.163630     edit     Change ONE snippet inside an existing file, leaving the rest untouched.
89412.163631     glob     List the files under a directory, by name.
89412.163632     grep     Search the CONTENTS of files under a directory with a regular expression, line by line.
89412.163633     read     Read a file in the workspace by workspace-relative `path`, OR a fetched document by `ref` (the id `web` returns).
89412.163634     recall   Search Marlowe's own memory: what the user said in earlier sessions, and what Marlowe has learned.
89412.163636     remember Ask the harness to record something worth keeping.
89412.163637     run      Delegate a sub-task to a child run and wait for it.
89412.163638     use      Find and load a skill.
89412.163639     web      Fetch one URL over https and return the page.
89412.163639     write    Create a file, or replace all of its contents.
89412.163641     Whether these ask depends on the trust tier this run was granted. The trust ledger that would raise a tier does not exist yet, so today they run at the tier the profile starts with.
89412.163642 
